  "modules.vocal-tract-frame.text.vocal_tract_geometry_is_generated_by_vocaltractlab_2_4_s_jd2_model_old_confi_485": "Vocal-tract geometry is generated by VocalTractLab 2.4's JD2 or W02 model. Old configurations are recomputed with the current model. Floor attachment is fixed to the jaw while the ventral endpoint moves. This approximation draws on Mills et al. 2019 (doi:10.1002/ca.23343) and 2020 (doi:10.1155/2020/1820978) interpretations of dynamic tissue folds; attachment position is a model setting. The page shows organ surfaces, geometric/synthesis areas, and transfer functions for one configuration. Tongue-position range and independent glottal height are project extensions; ranges describe model adjustability. Acoustic area corrections apply at some constrictions; mesh face count affects display detail.",
  "modules.vocal-tract-frame.text.external_head_shell_byzmod3d_3d_human_parts_pack_cc0_registered_schematicall_486": "External head shell: byzmod3d, 3D Human Parts Pack, CC0. Registered schematically for appearance; acoustic calculations use the selected vocal-tract model.",
  "modules.vocal-tract-frame.text.nasal_cavity_br_ning_et_al_2020_average_healthy_nasal_cavity_data_v4_cc_by_4_487": "Nasal cavity: Brüning et al., 2020, average healthy nasal-cavity data v4 (CC BY 4.0). All original mesh triangles are retained, coordinates transformed, and registered to JD2 as independent anatomical reference. Dashed sections indicate a neighboring nasal reference 5 mm off midline.",
  "modules.vocal-tract-frame.text.velum_and_uvula_are_reconstructed_from_native_configuration_and_dorsal_tissu_488": "Velum and uvula are reconstructed from native configuration and dorsal tissue thickness; 2D contours are cut from 3D surfaces.",
